## JSON attributes

Both attributes are computed. Read them with `jsondecode()`.

### activation_blockers_json

A JSON array of strings: why this revision cannot be promoted to notify mode yet. `null` when there are none.

### result_json

`AlertPreviewResultV1` as protobuf JSON with snake_case names. 64-bit integers are JSON strings, so wrap them in `tonumber()`, and fields at their zero value are left out, so read them with `try()`.

| Field | Type | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `status` | string | `passed` or `failed`. |
| `failure_reason` | string | Why a `failed` preview failed. |
| `requested_range_start`, `requested_range_end` | timestamp | The requested range, when one was given. |
| `requested_evidence_limit` | uint32 | Evidence samples requested, 1 to 64. Defaults to 64. |
| `canonical_config_hash` | string | Hash of the previewed revision's configuration. |
| `schedule_interval_seconds` | int64 | The alert's evaluation interval. |
| `configured_horizon_seconds` | int64 | The alert's `preview_horizon_seconds`, when set. |
| `sample_horizon_seconds` | int64 | History actually replayed. |
| `sample_interval_count` | int64 | Evaluation intervals replayed, at most 96. |
| `sample_contract` | string | Which intervals were replayed: `complete_most_recent_schedule_intervals`. |
| `evaluated_steps` | int64 | Intervals evaluated before a failure. |
| `horizon_complete` | bool | Whether the configured horizon was replayed in full. |
| `facts_complete` | bool | Whether every interval had complete telemetry facts. |
| `policy_resolution_purpose` | string | How routes were resolved: a routing prediction, never a delivery. |
| `activation_approval` | string | Always `not_granted`: a preview never approves notify mode. |
| `activation_signoff` | string | Always `not_created`. |
| `observed_firing_count` | int64 | Times the alert would have started firing. |
| `observed_routed_notification_count` | int64 | Notifications policies would have routed. |
| `projected_notifications_per_day` | int64 | `observed_routed_notification_count` scaled to a day and rounded up. |
| `projected_notifications_per_day_is_exact` | bool | Always `false`: the projection is an estimate. |
| `projection_hard_gate_applied` | bool | Whether enough notifications were observed for the projection to count. |
| `projection_confidence` | string | `observed_frequency` or `insufficient_sample`. |
| `projection_method` | string | The projection formula. |
| `projection_ratio` | object | `{ numerator_seconds_per_day, denominator_sample_horizon_seconds, rounding, upper_bound }`, the projection's inputs. |
| `predicted_firing_samples` | list(object) | Samples of evaluations that started firing, described below. |
| `predicted_notification_samples` | list(object) | Samples of evaluations that would have notified. |
| `predicted_firing_samples_truncated`, `predicted_notification_samples_truncated` | bool | Whether more samples existed than were kept. |
| `fact_summaries` | list(object) | Per-interval `{ evaluated_at, facts }`. `facts` reports the fact provider, errors, materialization, query cost, and pruning diagnostics, for troubleshooting. |

A sample, `AlertPreviewEventSampleV1`:

| Field | Type | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `evaluated_at` | timestamp | When the interval was evaluated. |
| `instance_key` | string | The alert instance. |
| `condition_state`, `lifecycle_state`, `routing_state` | string | States after the evaluation. |
| `should_notify` | bool | Whether it would have notified. |
| `selected_destination_ids` | list(string) | Destinations it would have reached. |
| `blocker_details` | list(object) | Each `{ code, message, remediation }`: what stopped a notification. |
| `blockers` | list(string) | The same blockers as messages only. |
| `reason` | string | Why the state changed. |

## Behaviour notes

- Set `revision_id` to the alert's `revision_id`. Without it the provider sends the same request key for every revision of the alert, and after the alert changes the server refuses the read because that key already belongs to the old revision.
- Reads with the same `definition_id`, `revision_id`, range, and `evidence_limit` return the same stored preview. Change one of them to run a new preview.
- `range_start` and `range_end` must be set together. Without them the preview replays the alert's `preview_horizon_seconds`, one day by default.
- `evidence_limit` is 1 to 64, and defaults to 64.
